# AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST, and that is the whole point of the file.
#
# The build context is the WORKING TREE, and .gitignore has no say in it. Under a denylist a new
# directory joins the context the day it is created, invisible in `git status` and unmentioned in any
# review: 67MB of assets/baked and assets/gen shipped to the daemon on every build for months that
# way. A denylist fails open, which for a build context means it fails silently and expensively.
#
# So: ignore EVERYTHING, then name what the two Dockerfiles actually COPY. A new directory is now
# absent from the context until somebody says otherwise, and the failure mode of forgetting is a build
# that stops with "not found" instead of one that quietly grows.
#
#   Dockerfile      (the site + docs apps): assets/vendor scripts generators harness/media/fonts.lock.json
#                   site (site/docker-start.sh included) docs-site NOTICE package.json package-lock.json (gsap)
#
# EDITING THIS FILE: add a COPY, add its `!` line here in the same commit. `make check GATE=docker-check` builds
# the context and prints what is in it.

**

# ── build inputs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/site/vendor-assets.mjs and scripts/vendor-gsap.mjs both live under scripts/.
!scripts
# generators/media/fonts.mjs refuses to run without its lock, and the builder stage runs it.
!harness/media/fonts.lock.json
!generators
!assets/vendor

# ── the two web apps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs-site runs on 3001 inside the SAME image and the site rewrites /docs to it. Its .source must
# stay out so the image regenerates it from content/ rather than shipping a stale copy.
!site
!docs-site
!NOTICE
# The engine's own package.json: site/lib/schema.ts imports it for the real description, version and
# licence in the SoftwareApplication JSON-LD. This is an allowlist (`**` then negations), so a file
# nobody thought to un-ignore is simply absent, which is how the first attempt at this shipped a
# build that died on "Module not found: Can't resolve '../../package.json'".
!package.json
# The root lockfile: both images run `npm ci --omit=dev` at /src|/engine so gsap's postinstall
# (scripts/vendor-gsap.mjs) can vendor assets/vendor/gsap.min.js, never committed (license).
!package-lock.json
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.next-build
**/.source
